
Day 73 :
Solved LeetCode 99 – Recover Binary Search Tree today!
- Approach:
A valid BST has an in-order traversal in sorted order.
I used in-order traversal to detect the two nodes that violate this ordering:
 Track the previous node. 
 When prev.val > current.val, a violation is found. 
 Identify the two incorrect nodes and swap their values at the end. 

Time: O(n) 
Space: O(h) for the recursion stack

-Takeaways:
 In-order traversal is extremely useful for BST problems. 
 A BST's structure can be validated through its sorted in-order sequence. 
 Learned how to recover a corrupted BST without changing its structure. 

